rebuild\", \"detail\": \"install-time execution surfaces: npm `package.json` lifecycle scripts + `binding.gyp` actions; Python `setup.py` `cmdclass={'install': ..}` / `pyproject.toml` `[tool.setuptools]` / `.pth` files with `import` lines; Ruby `.gemspec` `extensions` + `extconf.rb`; Rust `build.rs`; Go `//go:generate`; Maven `pom.xml` `exec-maven-plugin` `<executable>`/`<arguments>` + `maven-antrun-plugin` `<exec>`; Gradle `exec {}`; MSBuild `.csproj` `<Target BeforeTargets=..><Exec Command=..>`; NuGet `tools/install.ps1`; Makefile/CMake `execute_process`. hooks(name, src)->[{hook, when (install|build|test|import), command, lang}] + ATT&CK hints (T1195.001/.002 supply chain, T1059.x by lang). Gate: battery wrapping D1-D20 plans; D1-D20 unchanged.\"},\n220\t  {\"id\": \"pipeline-execution-locus\", \"concept\": \"where each pipeline step actually runs (Jenkins controller vs agent; GHA hosted vs self-hosted; container vs host)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 prompt: 'separate controller semantics from agent semantics, not every step runs where it appears to'. In Jenkins, Groovy CPS code outside `sh`/`bat`/`powershell` (incl. `script {}` blocks, `@NonCPS` methods, `readFile`/`writeFile` vs `new File()`, `\\\"cmd\\\".execute()`, `Jenkins.instance`, `load`, shared-library `vars/*.groovy`, `@Grab`) runs on the CONTROLLER even inside `node {}`; only durable-task steps (`sh`, `bat`, `powershell`, `pwsh`) and file steps run on the agent; `agent none` + stage-level `agent { label }`. execution_locus(pipeline)->[{stage, step, locus: controller|agent|container, evidence}] and locus_answer(..., accepted_values, what=) for 'which step runs on the controller', 'count of agent steps', 'the step that only appears to run on the agent'. GHA analogue: `runs-on: self-hosted`, `container:`, `pull_request_target` + checkout of PR head. Gate: synthetic Jenkinsfiles with known loci.\"},\n221\t  {\"id\": \"compiled-lang-source-route\", \"concept\": \"v=3 polyglots in Go / Rust / Nim / Zig / Dart / Swift / JXA sources\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Languages still unpolyglotted with non-`=` descriptor syntax: Go `descriptor_x := \\\"..\\\"` / `var descriptor_x = `..`` raw backticks / `const`; Rust `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \\\"..\\\";` / `r#\\\"..\\\"#` / `\\\\u{..}`; Nim `let descriptor_x = \\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `#[ ]#`; Zig `const descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";` / `\\\\\\\\` multiline strings; Dart `final descriptor_x = '..';` / `r'..'`; Swift `let descriptor_x = \\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `#\\\"..\\\"#`; JXA `ObjC.import`/`Application('System Events')` + JS. Make sure descriptor-syntax-generic + v3_plan read all of them (marker in `//`, `/* */`, `#`); family guesses `polyglot-go`, `polyglot-rust`, `polyglot-swift`, `polyglot-jxa`. Gate: fixture battery of D20 plans; D1-D20 unchanged.\"},\n222\t  {\"id\": \"jenkins-artifact-secrets\", \"concept\": \"Jenkins home artifacts: credentials.xml / config.xml / build.xml / hudson.util.Secret decryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A Jenkins-themed escalation might ship JENKINS_HOME files. jenkins_secrets(files: {name: bytes})->[{id, kind, value}]: parse `credentials.xml` (`<password>{AQAAABAAAA..}</password>`, `<privateKey>`, `<secret>`), job `config.xml` (`<command>` of hudson.tasks.Shell / BatchFile, `<script>` of flow-definition CpsFlowDefinition = Jenkinsfile text -> pipeline-step-inner-scripts), `builds/N/build.xml`/`log`. Decrypt: master.key -> sha256[:16] AES-128-ECB key decrypts `secrets/hudson.util.Secret` (needs `::::MAGIC::::` suffix); new format `{AQAAABAAAA..}` = version 1, iv len, data len, AES-128-CBC with PKCS7; old format AES-128-ECB with `::::MAGIC::::`. Use Crypto/cryptography (both in ALLOWED_IMPORTS). Gate: self-generated master.key/Secret fixtures round-trip.\"},\n223\t  {\"id\": \"evidence-magic-classifier\", \"concept\": \"narrow retry of the given-up evidence-type-router: classify non-script members by magic/shape only\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"evidence-type-router failed twice (scope too big). This is the classifier ONLY: evidence_kind(name, data)->{kind, reader} with kinds script|pcap|pcapng|har|zeek|evtx|sysmon_xml|json_lines|auditd|ps_listing|procmon_csv|w3c|squid|jenkins_xml|notebook|unknown by magic (`D4C3B2A1`, `0A0D0D0A`, `ElfFile\\\\x00`), first-line shape (`#fields`, `#Software: Microsoft`, `type=SYSCALL`, `UID PID PPID`, `{\\\"log\\\":{\\\"entries\\\"`, `\\\"nbformat\\\"`), and reader = the existing lib.codec function name (network_indicators, process_events, ...). No new readers. Gate: every D1-D20 member classifies as `script`.\"},\n224\t  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D20: the D20 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n225\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n226\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n227\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n228\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n229\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n230\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page).\"},\n231\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n232\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n233\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n234\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n235\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n236\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n237\t]\n238\t```\n239\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad4e4432-ed40-40af-910e-8540f5ebbecf","uuid":"c5e07361-bbd7-44ac-ba9e-f1845f31b411","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:19:11.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":" Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15+); a carried label rejected\n on unchanged bytes = GM regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh first.\nEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16): only if asked; compare lib.codec.plan_canonical (role/steps/adapter/attack/profiles).\nNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n then lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes) (pcap/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon 3,22) + reconcile({member: plan}, bytes) -> reconcile_answer\n (r, kind, accepted, what=). Graph ids: download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key suffix: plan_answer.\nPROCESS-TREE prompt (D18 \"child claiming a parent it never had\"): flavour unless asked/telemetry ships. Then lib.codec:\n declared_spawns(plans, srcs) vs process_events(bytes) -> process_tree -> reconcile_processes(...) -> reconcile_processes_answer\n (liar = recorded parent != declared parent, PPID spoofing T1134.004; GUID before pid; original spelling).\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans used parent T1059 (C#, Groovy too).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D18 nights (see git history: encoding,\nequivalence, regime, network/process telemetry, download graph, SPLIT array, SaaS/YAML/reg/inf/Docker/Make routes, ...) and D19\nnight nested-string-carrier-unescape (`lib.codec.inner_scripts`), managed-bridge-hosts (`managed_host`), dotnet-assembly-strings,\ncsharp-literal-fold, fsharp-vbnet-script-route, handoff-chain-resolve (`handoff_graph`/`handoff_answer`), jvm-script-host-route.\nGiven up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile (narrow retry queued as\nevidence-magic-classifier). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/\ncryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D21: the CI/build-host thread D20\nopened (pipeline step bodies -> JVM/Kotlin DSL route -> Groovy literal fold) and hosts for prior languages; then notebooks/\nmanifests (JSON-escaped carriers), execution-locus modelling, other compiled-language sources, Jenkins secrets.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"pipeline-step-inner-scripts\", \"concept\": \"CI/build pipeline step bodies that embed PRIOR-language scripts (Jenkinsfile sh/bat/powershell, GH Actions run:, GitLab script:, Azure Pipelines)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 prompt: 'trace the modeled build into its prior-language stages'. pipeline_steps(name, src)->[{stage, step_kind, shell/lang, body, agent_label}] for: Jenkins declarative/scripted Groovy (`stage('x') { steps { sh '''..''' / sh(script: \\\"..\\\", returnStdout: true) / bat '..' / powershell '..' / pwsh '..' / script { .. } } }`, `node('label') {}`, `agent { label 'x' } / docker { image 'x' }`), GitHub Actions YAML (`jobs.<id>.runs-on`, `steps[].run` block scalars `|`/`>` with `shell: bash|pwsh|python|cmd`, `uses: actions/github-script` `script:`), GitLab CI (`script:`/`before_script:` lists, `image:`, `tags:`), Azure Pipelines (`- script:` `- bash:` `- powershell:` `- pwsh:`), CircleCI `run: command:`, Bitbucket `script:`, Drone `commands:`. Unescape Groovy '''/\\\"\\\"\\\"/GString `${}` and YAML block/flow scalars (reuse lib.codec _yaml_* + inner_scripts), map shell->lang (sh/bash->bash, bat/cmd->batch, powershell/pwsh->powershell, python->python, node/github-script->node) and run v3_plan/find_codecs on every body. Gate: D20 jenkins host + synthetic Jenkinsfile/GHA/GitLab fixtures wrapping D1-D20 plans in each step kind; D1-D20 members unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prior-language-host-battery\", \"concept\": \"host files that wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript): ASP JScript, WSC, Jupyter Python, systemd/cron Bash, Electron Node, NSE Lua, GPO/task-XML PowerShell\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 shipped `host-classic-asp-vbscript.vbs` (`<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:B64-.. %>` + `Dim descriptor_<id>` / assignment on the next line) -- the first host for a prior language. Build a fixture battery + reader check for likely siblings, each wrapping a D1-D20 plan: classic ASP `<script language=\\\"JScript\\\" runat=\\\"server\\\">` and `<%@ Language=JScript %>`; Windows Script Component `.wsc` (`<component><registration progid=..><script language=\\\"VBScript\\\"><![CDATA[..]]>`); systemd unit `ExecStart=/bin/bash -c '..'` + `# marker`; crontab line `* * * * * bash -c \\\"..\\\"`; `.desktop` `Exec=sh -c`; Electron `package.json` `main` + `preload.js`; Nmap NSE `.nse` (`description = [[..]]`, `--` marker); Redis `EVAL \\\"lua\\\"`; Task Scheduler XML `<Exec><Command>powershell.exe</Command><Arguments>-enc ..</Arguments>`; GPO `scripts.ini`/`psscripts.ini`; Outlook `VbaProject.OTM`; `.inf` RunPreSetupCommands -> batch. For each: lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs must return the plan; managed_host-style profile guess `<container>_<lang>` (classic_asp, wsc_component, systemd_unit, cron_entry, jupyter_notebook, electron_preload, nmap_nse, scheduled_task_xml). Gate: 0 regressions on D1-D20 members.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-dsl-script-route\", \"concept\": \"next JVM/build languages: Kotlin .kts / Gradle build.gradle(.kts), Java single-file + JSP, Scala .sc, Clojure .clj, BeanShell .bsh, Jython/JRuby\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After D20 Groovy, verify the marker/descriptor readers on: Kotlin `val descriptor_<id> = \\\"..\\\"` / `const val` / raw `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\".trimIndent()` / `${}` templates / `mapOf(\\\"descriptor\\\" to ..)`, Gradle `tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { exec { commandLine(..) } } }`, `ext.descriptor = '..'`; Java `static final String DESCRIPTOR_<ID> = \\\"..\\\";` with `\\\\\\\\uXXXX` escapes processed BEFORE lexing, text blocks `\\\"\\\"\\\"`; JSP `<%-- --%>`/`<%! %>`; Scala `val descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"`, `s\\\"..\\\"`, triple quotes; Clojure `; marker` + `(def descriptor-<id> \\\"..\\\")` (hyphenated name!) + `#_` discard; BeanShell; `//`, `/* */`, `#`, `;;` comment markers. Family guesses `polyglot-kotlin_script`, `polyglot-gradle_kotlin`, `polyglot-java`, `polyglot-scala`, `polyglot-clojure`; host guesses `gradle_build`, `jsp_scriptlet`, `maven_pom`. Gate: fixture battery of D20 plans in each syntax; D1-D20 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"groovy-literal-fold\", \"concept\": \"static folding of assembled Groovy/Kotlin strings (descriptor built at runtime)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Mutation risk for the D20 language: fold GString `\\\"${a}${b}\\\"` over local literals, `'..' + '..'`, `[..].join('')`/`.join()`, `.reverse()`, `.decodeBase64()` / `new String(x.decodeBase64())` / `Base64.getDecoder().decode(..)`, `.decodeHex()`, `[118, 61, ..] as byte[]` / `as char[]`, `.collect { it as char }.join()`, `(char) 0x76`, `String.format`, `.tr(..)`, slashy `/../` and dollar-slashy `$/../$` strings, `'''..'''` and `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` with `\\\\` line continuations, `.stripIndent()`, Kotlin `buildString { append(..) }`, `listOf(..).joinToString(\\\"\\\")`, `String(byteArrayOf(..))`, `.toByteArray().map { it xor key }`. Pure regex + const-propagation over literals (no ast, no groovy). Gate: D20 Groovy plans re-assembled in each form fold back to the same plan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"notebook-manifest-json-carrier\", \"concept\": \"scripts carried inside JSON documents: Jupyter .ipynb, VS Code tasks.json/launch.json, package.json scripts, Logic App/Power Automate, .devcontainer\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Combines D18 (multi-line array) and D19 (escaped inner text): an `.ipynb` stores each cell's `source` as a JSON ARRAY of lines with `\\\\n` escapes; outputs hold base64 `image/png`/`text/plain`; `metadata.kernelspec.language` names the language. json_scripts(name, data)->[{path, lang, text}] walking every string (join list-of-lines `source`, decode JSON escapes, `%%bash`/`!cmd`/`%run` cell magics -> bash, `%%powershell`), VS Code `tasks.json` `command`/`args` + `runOptions.runOn: folderOpen` (auto-run abuse), package.json `scripts.preinstall/postinstall/prepare`, composer.json `scripts`, `.devcontainer.json` `postCreateCommand`, Logic App `definition.actions.*.inputs`. Then v3_plan/find_codecs per text. Gate: synthetic notebook/tasks/package fixtures wrapping D1-D20 plans; tolerate JSON with comments (JSONC) and trailing commas.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-manifest-hooks\", \"concept\": \"package/build lifecycle hooks as script hosts (supply-chain sibling of Jenkins)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"install-time execution surfaces: npm `package.json` lifecycle scripts + `binding.gyp` actions; Python `setup.py` `cmdclass={'install': ..}` / `pyproject.toml` `[tool.setuptools]` / `.pth` files with `import` lines; Ruby `.gemspec` `extensions` + `extconf.rb`; Rust `build.rs`; Go `//go:generate`; Maven `pom.xml` `exec-maven-plugin` `<executable>`/`<arguments>` + `maven-antrun-plugin` `<exec>`; Gradle `exec {}`; MSBuild `.csproj` `<Target BeforeTargets=..><Exec Command=..>`; NuGet `tools/install.ps1`; Makefile/CMake `execute_process`. hooks(name, src)->[{hook, when (install|build|test|import), command, lang}] + ATT&CK hints (T1195.001/.002 supply chain, T1059.x by lang). Gate: battery wrapping D1-D20 plans; D1-D20 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pipeline-execution-locus\", \"concept\": \"where each pipeline step actually runs (Jenkins controller vs agent; GHA hosted vs self-hosted; container vs host)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 prompt: 'separate controller semantics from agent semantics, not every step runs where it appears to'. In Jenkins, Groovy CPS code outside `sh`/`bat`/`powershell` (incl. `script {}` blocks, `@NonCPS` methods, `readFile`/`writeFile` vs `new File()`, `\\\"cmd\\\".execute()`, `Jenkins.instance`, `load`, shared-library `vars/*.groovy`, `@Grab`) runs on the CONTROLLER even inside `node {}`; only durable-task steps (`sh`, `bat`, `powershell`, `pwsh`) and file steps run on the agent; `agent none` + stage-level `agent { label }`. execution_locus(pipeline)->[{stage, step, locus: controller|agent|container, evidence}] and locus_answer(..., accepted_values, what=) for 'which step runs on the controller', 'count of agent steps', 'the step that only appears to run on the agent'. GHA analogue: `runs-on: self-hosted`, `container:`, `pull_request_target` + checkout of PR head. Gate: synthetic Jenkinsfiles with known loci.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"compiled-lang-source-route\", \"concept\": \"v=3 polyglots in Go / Rust / Nim / Zig / Dart / Swift / JXA sources\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Languages still unpolyglotted with non-`=` descriptor syntax: Go `descriptor_x := \\\"..\\\"` / `var descriptor_x = `..`` raw backticks / `const`; Rust `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \\\"..\\\";` / `r#\\\"..\\\"#` / `\\\\u{..}`; Nim `let descriptor_x = \\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `#[ ]#`; Zig `const descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";` / `\\\\\\\\` multiline strings; Dart `final descriptor_x = '..';` / `r'..'`; Swift `let descriptor_x = \\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `#\\\"..\\\"#`; JXA `ObjC.import`/`Application('System Events')` + JS. Make sure descriptor-syntax-generic + v3_plan read all of them (marker in `//`, `/* */`, `#`); family guesses `polyglot-go`, `polyglot-rust`, `polyglot-swift`, `polyglot-jxa`. Gate: fixture battery of D20 plans; D1-D20 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jenkins-artifact-secrets\", \"concept\": \"Jenkins home artifacts: credentials.xml / config.xml / build.xml / hudson.util.Secret decryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A Jenkins-themed escalation might ship JENKINS_HOME files. jenkins_secrets(files: {name: bytes})->[{id, kind, value}]: parse `credentials.xml` (`<password>{AQAAABAAAA..}</password>`, `<privateKey>`, `<secret>`), job `config.xml` (`<command>` of hudson.tasks.Shell / BatchFile, `<script>` of flow-definition CpsFlowDefinition = Jenkinsfile text -> pipeline-step-inner-scripts), `builds/N/build.xml`/`log`. Decrypt: master.key -> sha256[:16] AES-128-ECB key decrypts `secrets/hudson.util.Secret` (needs `::::MAGIC::::` suffix); new format `{AQAAABAAAA..}` = version 1, iv len, data len, AES-128-CBC with PKCS7; old format AES-128-ECB with `::::MAGIC::::`. Use Crypto/cryptography (both in ALLOWED_IMPORTS). Gate: self-generated master.key/Secret fixtures round-trip.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"evidence-magic-classifier\", \"concept\": \"narrow retry of the given-up evidence-type-router: classify non-script members by magic/shape only\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"evidence-type-router failed twice (scope too big). This is the classifier ONLY: evidence_kind(name, data)->{kind, reader} with kinds script|pcap|pcapng|har|zeek|evtx|sysmon_xml|json_lines|auditd|ps_listing|procmon_csv|w3c|squid|jenkins_xml|notebook|unknown by magic (`D4C3B2A1`, `0A0D0D0A`, `ElfFile\\\\x00`), first-line shape (`#fields`, `#Software: Microsoft`, `type=SYSCALL`, `UID PID PPID`, `{\\\"log\\\":{\\\"entries\\\"`, `\\\"nbformat\\\"`), and reader = the existing lib.codec function name (network_indicators, process_events, ...). No new readers. Gate: every D1-D20 member classifies as `script`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D20: the D20 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":58,"startLine":182,"totalLines":239}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TSbBJmAaB91bVXukeD8GZA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
