{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QzoP28fbM6yAB7vo6tNsA1","type":"tool_result","content":"38\t  `evidence-01.zip` holding every `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n39\t  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n40\t\n41\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\n42\tEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\n43\tMastery cycle; D16: runner timeouts only). **D17-D21: no axis** -- TT/Mastery first try, 0 new VARIANT AXIS lines, `novel_labels:\n44\t{}`; each day's new carrier shape (D18 SPLIT array, D19 escaped-nested ASPX, D20 plain Groovy/ASP one-liners, D21 YAML `#`\n45\tmarker + `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`) was identical in every mode, only values re-rolled. D20 auto cases (TT 717b8371, Mastery\n46\t1478867c) and D21 (TT f01e0ff9, Mastery 2620b793) are value re-rolls only.\n47\t- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n48\t  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n49\t  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; D16+ every mode incl. the single): label the JOIN\n50\t  STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool; bare `call set\n51\t  \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent.\n52\t  Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.\n53\t  label_regime`/`label_expansion`); old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different\n54\t  labels, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) at once.\n55\t- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n56\t  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n57\t  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n58\t  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n59\t- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n60\t  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n61\t- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n62\t  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D17, only\n63\t  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n64\t  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n65\t  **D18 `SPLIT` is a LAYOUT tag, not an encoding**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` stands alone on its line and the data is the\n66\t  next multi-line literal array `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\"<TAG>-chunk\", \"chunk\", ..].join(\"\")`; the real tag\n67\t  (FRAG/HEX/HB64/B64) is the first chunk's prefix, and `buildAnalysisPlan_<id>()` holds an untagged copy (`const encoded_<id> =\n68\t  [..].join(\"\")`). Parse rule: if the marker match has no data, join every all-literal array / concat run in the file\n69\t  (quotes `\"` `'` and backticks), strip a leading `[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-`, peel; keep the one that yields `v=`. Patched in the\n70\t  D18 solve.py (`_v3` candidates); lib.codec.v3_plan handles it since the D18-night prebuild.\n71\t- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF ScriptText, D19 ASPX)** -- the whole inner script is a string literal of the host:\n72\t  `<%@ Page Language=\"C#\" %><script runat=\"server\"> private static readonly string EmbeddedCsx_<8hex> = \"// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:\n73\t  HEX-<data>\\n#nullable enable\\n..string descriptor_<id> = \\\"<data>\\\";\\n\";`. In raw bytes the marker data runs on into a\n74\t  literal `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is `\\\"`-quoted, so the carried regexes find nothing. Parse rule: when a v=3 file\n75\t  yields no plan, unescape string-literal escapes (`\\n \\\" \\\\ \\t`, C# verbatim `\"\"`, VB `\"\"`, XML `&quot;`/CDATA, JSON\n76\t  `\\u0022`) and rescan; or stop marker data at `\\`. `lib.codec.v3_plan` already decoded the D19 ASPX file at solve time\n77\t  (the carried solve.py did not call it) -- **fall back to lib.codec.v3_plan before anything else**.\n78\t- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n79\t  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt, AutoHotkey), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n80\t  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n81\t  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16),\n82\t  **`descriptor_<8hex> := \"..\"` AutoHotkey v2 (D17)**, C# `string descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";` + `BuildPlan_<id>() => new\n83\t  Dictionary<string,string> { [\"descriptor\"] = .. }` (D19), Apps Script `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` +\n84\t  `Object.freeze({ descriptor: encoded_<id> })` (D18), Groovy `final String descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` + `def buildPlan_<id> = { ->\n85\t  [descriptor: ..].asImmutable() }` (D20), classic ASP `Dim descriptor_<8hex>` then `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` on the NEXT line\n86\t  inside `<% %>` with a `'` marker (D20), **YAML `env:` key `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \"..\"` -- UPPERCASE, NO `_<id>` suffix**,\n87\t  `#` marker on line 1 (D21 GH Actions). Never anchor on `=` / `:=` / `set` / `<-` -- parse rule: regex\n88\t  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, any comment syntax/case/extension; if the data group\n89\t  is empty (`SPLIT`), fall through to the literal-array join above.\n90\t- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix: decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read by `parseInt(x, R)`/`int(x, R)` --\n91\t  READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE (keys too); base64 standard AND urlsafe (whitelist + pad); reversal of the LIST\n92\t  (`reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list`) vs the TEXT (`reversed_base64`) -- try both; material as one literal, split chunks,\n93\t  `+=`, adjacent strings, `.`-FRAG, D18 multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` -- join first; same-language carrier may be a frozen exe (D6\n94\t  cx_Freeze) -- locate by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), never by file type.\n95\t- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n96\t  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n97\t- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n98\t  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery hit the 60 s local `hb_timed` cap (fixed: D17-D19 Mastery 12-18 s, start+submit\n99\t  ~70 % of it, solve 0.5-5.6 s). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n100\t\n101\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n102\t| You see | First move |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad4e4432-ed40-40af