{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTCeEr4vXUDqSMjzmiz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011N77dPoXiNuUjWiNjNvLmh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=s[i:]\njb=old.index(\"```json\")+len(\"```json\"); je=old.index(\"```\",jb)\noldg={g['id']:g for g in json.loads(old[jb:je])}\nkeep_ids=[\"build-manifest-hooks\",\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\",\"php-cli\",\"lua-unluac\",\"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\",\"leaf-ext-list\",\"new-synthetic-label-family\",\"family-name-underscore\",\"tcl-r-interpreters\",\"applescript-scpt\",\"js-deob-extras\",\"ps-deob-modules\",\"xlm-standalone\",\"dotnet-script\"]\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"gha-trigger-trust-model\",\"concept\":\"GitHub Actions trigger / permission / runner trust-boundary model (who can trigger a workflow, which runner and token inherit the trust)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 prompt: 'decides who can trigger it and which runner inherits the trust. Identify each trigger and trust boundary'. D21 bytes were all `on: workflow_dispatch:` + `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, so a variant/next day adding real triggers would ask new suffixes (`-trigger`, `-runner`, `-trust-boundary`, `-permissions`). Build gha_workflow(name, src)->{name, triggers:[event names incl. filters], jobs:[{id, runs_on, self_hosted(bool), container, environment, permissions (workflow- and job-level, 'write-all'/'read-all'/map), needs, if, steps:[{name, uses, run, shell, with, env}]}], secrets_used, untrusted_contexts} with a regex/indent YAML walk (reuse lib.codec _yaml_* helpers; PyYAML 1.1 turns `on:` into True -- accept both `on`/`'on'`/`true` keys if a parser is used). Trust labels: privileged-trigger set {pull_request_target, workflow_run, issue_comment, issues, discussion*, fork PR via pull_request_target + checkout of `github.event.pull_request.head.(sha|ref)`}, runner trust {github-hosted, self-hosted (any label list containing self-hosted), container}, token scope (none/read/write per key). gha_answer(model, field, accepted_values, what=) maps to enums by original spelling. Gate: synthetic workflows covering each trigger form (`on: push`, `on: [push, pull_request]`, map with filters, `schedule`, `workflow_call`) + the D21 members (triggers=['workflow_dispatch'], runner github-hosted).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-schedule-persistence-model\",\"concept\":\"'the job that keeps coming back': schedule / re-trigger persistence across CI, OS and orchestrator descriptors\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 base id `github-actions-persistence` + prompt 'find the job that keeps coming back' -- not in the bytes yet. schedule_entries(name, src)->[{kind, expr, period_s (best effort), target(job/command), lang, attack}] for GHA `on: schedule: - cron: '..'` (5-field POSIX cron, UTC), `workflow_run: workflows: [..] types: [completed]` self/cyclic chains (graph cycle = keeps coming back), `repository_dispatch` + a step that calls the dispatches API, GitLab `rules: - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \\\"schedule\\\"'`, Azure `schedules: - cron:`, K8s `kind: CronJob spec.schedule`, systemd `.timer` OnCalendar/OnBootSec/OnUnitActiveSec + `Restart=always`, crontab/`/etc/cron.d` lines incl. `@reboot`, launchd plist StartInterval/StartCalendarInterval/RunAtLoad/KeepAlive, Task Scheduler XML triggers (TimeTrigger Repetition Interval PT5M, LogonTrigger, BootTrigger), WMI __IntervalTimerInstruction/__EventFilter WITHIN n, Run/RunOnce keys. ATT&CK: T1053.003 cron, .005 schtasks, .006 systemd timers, .007 container orchestration job, T1543.001 launch agent/.002 systemd service/.004 launch daemon, T1546.003 WMI, T1547.001 Run keys; CI persistence via workflow file = T1098/T1195.002 hint only. persistence_answer(entries, field, accepted_values). Gate: fixtures per kind + every D1-D21 member returns [].\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-yaml-sibling-route\",\"concept\":\"next CI YAML languages after D21 GitHub Actions: GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI, Bitbucket, Drone, Buildkite, Tekton\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA; the CI sibling is the likeliest next language. Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs + pipeline_steps on a fixture battery wrapping D21 plans: GitLab `.gitlab-ci.yml` (`variables: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \\\"..\\\"` top-level or per-job, `script:`/`before_script:` lists, `include:`, `extends:`, `!reference [..]`), Azure `azure-pipelines.yml` (`variables: - name: X value: ..` list form AND map form, `- script:`/`- bash:`/`- powershell:`/`- pwsh:`/`- task: PowerShell@2 inputs: script:`), CircleCI (`environment:`, `run: command: |`, orbs), Bitbucket (`pipelines: default: - step: script:`), Drone (`commands:`), Buildkite (`command:`), Tekton (`steps[].script:`). Descriptor may be UPPERCASE without an id (D21 HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR) -- accept `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR(_\\\\w+)?` and `descriptor_\\\\w+` keys in env/variables/environment maps. Family guesses `polyglot-gitlab_ci`, `polyglot-azure_pipelines`, `polyglot-circleci`. Gate: D1-D21 members unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"github-action-definition-route\",\"concept\":\"GitHub action definitions and reusable workflows as the 'static handoff into the next language'\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 prompt: 'follow the static handoff into the next language'. action_handoffs(members: {name: text})->[{from, via, to_lang, body_or_target}]: `action.yml`/`action.yaml` `runs: using: composite` (steps run+shell), `using: node16|node20|node24` + `main:`/`pre:`/`post:` JS entry (resolve to a member, route as JS/TS), `using: docker` + `image: Dockerfile|docker://` + `entrypoint:`/`args:` (route Dockerfile via lib.codec Docker route); workflows `uses: ./.github/actions/x` (local, resolve), `uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/x.yml@ref` (`on: workflow_call` reusable, `inputs:`/`secrets: inherit`), `uses: actions/github-script@v7` `with: script: |` (JS body), `run:` with `shell: bash|pwsh|powershell|python|cmd|sh` or custom `shell: perl {0}` -> language. Map to next_language spellings used by v=3 plans (powershell, jscript/node, batch, vbscript, python, bash). Gate: synthetic repo trees + D21 members (no handoff, only `run: ':'`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-expression-injection-secrets\",\"concept\":\"GitHub/GitLab expression contexts: untrusted input interpolated into run bodies, secrets/token exposure\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Trust-boundary questions may ask which step is injectable or which secret leaks. ci_expressions(src)->[{job, step, field, expr, context_root, untrusted(bool), sink (run/script/with.script/env)}] over `${{ .. }}` (GHA) and `$VAR`/`${VAR}` + `$CI_*` (GitLab): untrusted roots github.event.(issue|pull_request|comment|review|review_comment|discussion|pages|commits|head_commit).*(title|body|name|message|label|ref|email|default_branch|head_ref), github.head_ref; secrets.*, GITHUB_TOKEN, ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_*, `echo \\\"::add-mask::\\\"`, writes to $GITHUB_ENV/$GITHUB_OUTPUT/$GITHUB_PATH (env injection), `pull_request_target` + checkout + run (pwn request). ATT&CK hints T1059.004 injection sink, T1552.001/.004/.007, T1528. Gate: fixtures with known injectable steps; D21 members -> [].\"},\n {\"id\":\"k8s-helm-manifest-route\",\"concept\":\"Kubernetes / Helm / Kustomize manifests carrying scripts (CronJob, Job, DaemonSet, ConfigMap, Secret)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Orchestration sibling of CI YAML and the cleanest 'keeps coming back' carrier (T1053.007). k8s_scripts(name, src)->[{doc_index, kind, name, container, command, args, script_lang, schedule}] over multi-doc `---`: `spec.(template.)spec.containers[].command/args` (`[\\\"/bin/sh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` flow or block lists), `jobTemplate` for CronJob + `spec.schedule`, ConfigMap `data:` script blocks (`|`), Secret `data:` base64 (decode) / `stringData:`, `initContainers`, `lifecycle.postStart.exec.command`, hostPath/privileged flags (trust boundary). Helm: strip `{{ .. }}`/`{{- .. -}}`, fold `{{ \\\"..\\\" | b64dec }}` / `b64enc` over literals, `.Values` lookups from a values.yaml member. Then v3_plan/find_codecs per body. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cloud-iac-userdata-route\",\"concept\":\"IaC templates with embedded scripts: Terraform local-exec/user_data, CloudFormation UserData Fn::Base64, ARM/Bicep deploymentScripts, Ansible shell tasks\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"After CI, infra-as-code is the next 'build that runs code' surface. iac_scripts(name, src)->[{resource, field, lang, body}]: Terraform HCL `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT interpreter = [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\"] }`, `user_data = base64encode(..)`/`filebase64(..)`/`templatefile`, `data \\\"external\\\" { program = [..] }`; CloudFormation YAML/JSON `UserData: Fn::Base64: !Sub |` (short-form tags `!Sub`/`!Join`/`!Base64` -- tag-tolerant walk), `AWS::SSM::Document` `runCommand`; ARM JSON `Microsoft.Resources/deploymentScripts` `properties.scriptContent` + `kind: AzurePowerShell|AzureCLI`, Bicep `scriptContent: '''..'''`; Ansible `ansible.builtin.shell/command/script/raw/win_shell` (`args: executable:`), `become:`. Heredoc/`'''` joins, `${var}` interpolation left as-is. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\",\"concept\":\"YAML-specific carrier mutations for the D21 language: block/folded scalars, anchors/aliases, tags, escapes, multi-doc\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 carriers were a one-line quoted scalar; the next twist on a YAML language (as D18/D19 twisted theirs) would hide the descriptor in YAML semantics. yaml_scalar(src, key)->decoded text honoring: literal `|`/`|-`/`|+` (keep newlines) vs folded `>`/`>-` (lines JOIN WITH A SPACE -- strip spaces before peeling hex/base64), indentation indicators `|2`, double-quoted escapes (`\\\\x41` `\\\\u0041` `\\\\U..` `\\\\n`, line-folding with trailing `\\\\`), single-quoted `''`, plain multi-line scalars, anchors `&d` + aliases `*d` + merge keys `<<: *base` (descriptor defined in one job, used in another), `!!binary` (base64 -> bytes), `!!str`, flow maps/sequences `{X: \\\"..\\\"}`/`[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]` with a join step, comments after values, multi-document `---`/`...`, CRLF. Also the marker split across several `#` comment lines. Gate: each twist applied to the D21 members peels back to the same plan; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"git-repo-hooks-route\",\"concept\":\"repository-level auto-run surfaces: git hooks, filter/diff drivers, husky, pre-commit, devcontainer, submodules\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Supply-chain persistence next to CI: repo_hooks(members)->[{surface, trigger, command, lang}]: `.git/hooks/{pre-commit,post-checkout,post-merge,pre-push}` (shebang -> lang), `.git/config` `[core] hooksPath`, `[filter \\\"x\\\"] clean/smudge = ..` + `.gitattributes` `* filter=x`, `[diff \\\"x\\\"] textconv`, `[core] fsmonitor = ..`, `.husky/*`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` `repos[].hooks[].entry` + `language:`, `.gitmodules` url/update=!cmd, `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` postCreate/postStart (reuse json_scripts), `.vscode/tasks.json` `runOn: folderOpen`. ATT&CK hints T1195.002, T1546 (event-triggered), T1059.x. Gate: synthetic repo fixtures; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"launchd-plist-route\",\"concept\":\"macOS launchd / plist persistence (XML and binary plist)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"OS-side 'keeps coming back' sibling of D13 AppleScript. plist_scripts(name, data)->[{label, program_arguments, run_at_load, keep_alive, start_interval, lang}] for XML plists (`<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/bin/sh</string><string>-c</string><string>..</string>`) and binary `bplist00` (pure-Python parser: offset table, object refs; ints, strings ASCII/UTF-16BE, arrays, dicts, data, bools), `LaunchAgents`/`LaunchDaemons` path hints, `osascript -e` bodies -> AppleScript route. ATT&CK T1543.001/.004, T1647. Gate: plistlib-generated XML+binary fixtures round-trip (plistlib is stdlib; check ALLOWED_IMPORTS, else hand-parse).\"}\n]\nfor k in keep_ids: assert k in oldg, k\nkept=[oldg[k] for k in keep_ids]\nfor g in kept:\n    if g['id']=='build-manifest-hooks':\n        g['priority']=2; g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\"D1-D20\",\"D1-D21\")+\" (Retry after 1 failed attempt on D20 night: keep the scope to manifest parsing + hook listing; reuse json_scripts/pipeline_steps rather than new parsers.)\"\n    if g['id']=='solver-lib-v3-fallback':\n        g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\"STILL OPEN after D20: the D20 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20 needed none because every carrier was plain).\",\"STILL OPEN after D21: the D21 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D21 needed none because every carrier was plain).\")\n    if g['id']=='family-name-underscore':\n        g['detail']+=\" D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file.\"\n    if g['id']=='leaf-ext-list':\n        g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\".gs .csx .groovy (and future\",\".gs .csx .groovy .yml (and future\").replace(\" .yml .tf\",\" .tf\")\ngaps=new[:4]+[kept[0]]+new[4:8]+[kept[1]]+kept[2:]+new[8:]\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}, g['id']\nhdr=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D19 nights (see git history) and D20 night\npipeline-step-inner-scripts (`pipeline_steps`), prior-language-host-battery, jvm-dsl-script-route, groovy-literal-fold,\nnotebook-manifest-json-carrier (`json_scripts`), pipeline-execution-locus (`execution_locus`/`locus_answer`),\ncompiled-lang-source-route, jenkins-artifact-secrets, evidence-magic-classifier (`evidence_kind`). Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile. build-manifest-hooks failed once (retry\nqueued). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/\nEvtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D22: the D21 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n(GHA trigger/trust model, schedule persistence), the next CI YAML sibling, GitHub action/reusable-workflow handoffs; then\ninjection/secrets, k8s/IaC carriers, YAML carrier twists, repo hooks, launchd.\n\n```json\n\"\"\"+json.dumps(gaps,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False).replace('[{\"id\"','[\\n  {\"id\"').replace('}, {\"id\"','},\\n  {\"id\"').replace('}]','}\\n]')+\"\\n```\\n\"\ns=s[:i]+hdr\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n# validate\nt=open(p).read(); a=t.index(\"```json\")+7; b=t.index(\"```\",a); g=json.loads(t[a:b]); print(len(g), [x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild'])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":814,"cache_read_input_tokens":113186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":814},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad4e4432-ed40-40af-910e-8540f5ebbecf","uuid":"d22393dd-941d-4ee4-a3c4-3697145bc9c5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:22:49.613Z","request_id":"req_011CgFTCdpJ2avk3HhnRNvZG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011N77dPoXiNuUjWiNjNvLmh":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=s[i:]\njb=old.index(\"```json\")+len(\"```json\"); je=old.index(\"```\",jb)\noldg={g['id']:g for g in json.loads(old[jb:je])}\nkeep_ids=[\"build-manifest-hooks\",\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\",\"php-cli\",\"lua-unluac\",\"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\",\"leaf-ext-list\",\"new-synthetic-label-family\",\"family-name-underscore\",\"tcl-r-interpreters\",\"applescript-scpt\",\"js-deob-extras\",\"ps-deob-modules\",\"xlm-standalone\",\"dotnet-script\"]\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"gha-trigger-trust-model\",\"concept\":\"GitHub Actions trigger / permission / runner trust-boundary model (who can trigger a workflow, which runner and token inherit the trust)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 prompt: 'decides who can trigger it and which runner inherits the trust. Identify each trigger and trust boundary'. D21 bytes were all `on: workflow_dispatch:` + `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, so a variant/next day adding real triggers would ask new suffixes (`-trigger`, `-runner`, `-trust-boundary`, `-permissions`). Build gha_workflow(name, src)->{name, triggers:[event names incl. filters], jobs:[{id, runs_on, self_hosted(bool), container, environment, permissions (workflow- and job-level, 'write-all'/'read-all'/map), needs, if, steps:[{name, uses, run, shell, with, env}]}], secrets_used, untrusted_contexts} with a regex/indent YAML walk (reuse lib.codec _yaml_* helpers; PyYAML 1.1 turns `on:` into True -- accept both `on`/`'on'`/`true` keys if a parser is used). Trust labels: privileged-trigger set {pull_request_target, workflow_run, issue_comment, issues, discussion*, fork PR via pull_request_target + checkout of `github.event.pull_request.head.(sha|ref)`}, runner trust {github-hosted, self-hosted (any label list containing self-hosted), container}, token scope (none/read/write per key). gha_answer(model, field, accepted_values, what=) maps to enums by original spelling. Gate: synthetic workflows covering each trigger form (`on: push`, `on: [push, pull_request]`, map with filters, `schedule`, `workflow_call`) + the D21 members (triggers=['workflow_dispatch'], runner github-hosted).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-schedule-persistence-model\",\"concept\":\"'the job that keeps coming back': schedule / re-trigger persistence across CI, OS and orchestrator descriptors\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 base id `github-actions-persistence` + prompt 'find the job that keeps coming back' -- not in the bytes yet. schedule_entries(name, src)->[{kind, expr, period_s (best effort), target(job/command), lang, attack}] for GHA `on: schedule: - cron: '..'` (5-field POSIX cron, UTC), `workflow_run: workflows: [..] types: [completed]` self/cyclic chains (graph cycle = keeps coming back), `repository_dispatch` + a step that calls the dispatches API, GitLab `rules: - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \\\"schedule\\\"'`, Azure `schedules: - cron:`, K8s `kind: CronJob spec.schedule`, systemd `.timer` OnCalendar/OnBootSec/OnUnitActiveSec + `Restart=always`, crontab/`/etc/cron.d` lines incl. `@reboot`, launchd plist StartInterval/StartCalendarInterval/RunAtLoad/KeepAlive, Task Scheduler XML triggers (TimeTrigger Repetition Interval PT5M, LogonTrigger, BootTrigger), WMI __IntervalTimerInstruction/__EventFilter WITHIN n, Run/RunOnce keys. ATT&CK: T1053.003 cron, .005 schtasks, .006 systemd timers, .007 container orchestration job, T1543.001 launch agent/.002 systemd service/.004 launch daemon, T1546.003 WMI, T1547.001 Run keys; CI persistence via workflow file = T1098/T1195.002 hint only. persistence_answer(entries, field, accepted_values). Gate: fixtures per kind + every D1-D21 member returns [].\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-yaml-sibling-route\",\"concept\":\"next CI YAML languages after D21 GitHub Actions: GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI, Bitbucket, Drone, Buildkite, Tekton\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA; the CI sibling is the likeliest next language. Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs + pipeline_steps on a fixture battery wrapping D21 plans: GitLab `.gitlab-ci.yml` (`variables: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \\\"..\\\"` top-level or per-job, `script:`/`before_script:` lists, `include:`, `extends:`, `!reference [..]`), Azure `azure-pipelines.yml` (`variables: - name: X value: ..` list form AND map form, `- script:`/`- bash:`/`- powershell:`/`- pwsh:`/`- task: PowerShell@2 inputs: script:`), CircleCI (`environment:`, `run: command: |`, orbs), Bitbucket (`pipelines: default: - step: script:`), Drone (`commands:`), Buildkite (`command:`), Tekton (`steps[].script:`). Descriptor may be UPPERCASE without an id (D21 HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR) -- accept `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR(_\\\\w+)?` and `descriptor_\\\\w+` keys in env/variables/environment maps. Family guesses `polyglot-gitlab_ci`, `polyglot-azure_pipelines`, `polyglot-circleci`. Gate: D1-D21 members unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"github-action-definition-route\",\"concept\":\"GitHub action definitions and reusable workflows as the 'static handoff into the next language'\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 prompt: 'follow the static handoff into the next language'. action_handoffs(members: {name: text})->[{from, via, to_lang, body_or_target}]: `action.yml`/`action.yaml` `runs: using: composite` (steps run+shell), `using: node16|node20|node24` + `main:`/`pre:`/`post:` JS entry (resolve to a member, route as JS/TS), `using: docker` + `image: Dockerfile|docker://` + `entrypoint:`/`args:` (route Dockerfile via lib.codec Docker route); workflows `uses: ./.github/actions/x` (local, resolve), `uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/x.yml@ref` (`on: workflow_call` reusable, `inputs:`/`secrets: inherit`), `uses: actions/github-script@v7` `with: script: |` (JS body), `run:` with `shell: bash|pwsh|powershell|python|cmd|sh` or custom `shell: perl {0}` -> language. Map to next_language spellings used by v=3 plans (powershell, jscript/node, batch, vbscript, python, bash). Gate: synthetic repo trees + D21 members (no handoff, only `run: ':'`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ci-expression-injection-secrets\",\"concept\":\"GitHub/GitLab expression contexts: untrusted input interpolated into run bodies, secrets/token exposure\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Trust-boundary questions may ask which step is injectable or which secret leaks. ci_expressions(src)->[{job, step, field, expr, context_root, untrusted(bool), sink (run/script/with.script/env)}] over `${{ .. }}` (GHA) and `$VAR`/`${VAR}` + `$CI_*` (GitLab): untrusted roots github.event.(issue|pull_request|comment|review|review_comment|discussion|pages|commits|head_commit).*(title|body|name|message|label|ref|email|default_branch|head_ref), github.head_ref; secrets.*, GITHUB_TOKEN, ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_*, `echo \\\"::add-mask::\\\"`, writes to $GITHUB_ENV/$GITHUB_OUTPUT/$GITHUB_PATH (env injection), `pull_request_target` + checkout + run (pwn request). ATT&CK hints T1059.004 injection sink, T1552.001/.004/.007, T1528. Gate: fixtures with known injectable steps; D21 members -> [].\"},\n {\"id\":\"k8s-helm-manifest-route\",\"concept\":\"Kubernetes / Helm / Kustomize manifests carrying scripts (CronJob, Job, DaemonSet, ConfigMap, Secret)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Orchestration sibling of CI YAML and the cleanest 'keeps coming back' carrier (T1053.007). k8s_scripts(name, src)->[{doc_index, kind, name, container, command, args, script_lang, schedule}] over multi-doc `---`: `spec.(template.)spec.containers[].command/args` (`[\\\"/bin/sh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` flow or block lists), `jobTemplate` for CronJob + `spec.schedule`, ConfigMap `data:` script blocks (`|`), Secret `data:` base64 (decode) / `stringData:`, `initContainers`, `lifecycle.postStart.exec.command`, hostPath/privileged flags (trust boundary). Helm: strip `{{ .. }}`/`{{- .. -}}`, fold `{{ \\\"..\\\" | b64dec }}` / `b64enc` over literals, `.Values` lookups from a values.yaml member. Then v3_plan/find_codecs per body. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cloud-iac-userdata-route\",\"concept\":\"IaC templates with embedded scripts: Terraform local-exec/user_data, CloudFormation UserData Fn::Base64, ARM/Bicep deploymentScripts, Ansible shell tasks\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"After CI, infra-as-code is the next 'build that runs code' surface. iac_scripts(name, src)->[{resource, field, lang, body}]: Terraform HCL `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT interpreter = [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\"] }`, `user_data = base64encode(..)`/`filebase64(..)`/`templatefile`, `data \\\"external\\\" { program = [..] }`; CloudFormation YAML/JSON `UserData: Fn::Base64: !Sub |` (short-form tags `!Sub`/`!Join`/`!Base64` -- tag-tolerant walk), `AWS::SSM::Document` `runCommand`; ARM JSON `Microsoft.Resources/deploymentScripts` `properties.scriptContent` + `kind: AzurePowerShell|AzureCLI`, Bicep `scriptContent: '''..'''`; Ansible `ansible.builtin.shell/command/script/raw/win_shell` (`args: executable:`), `become:`. Heredoc/`'''` joins, `${var}` interpolation left as-is. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\",\"concept\":\"YAML-specific carrier mutations for the D21 language: block/folded scalars, anchors/aliases, tags, escapes, multi-doc\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 carriers were a one-line quoted scalar; the next twist on a YAML language (as D18/D19 twisted theirs) would hide the descriptor in YAML semantics. yaml_scalar(src, key)->decoded text honoring: literal `|`/`|-`/`|+` (keep newlines) vs folded `>`/`>-` (lines JOIN WITH A SPACE -- strip spaces before peeling hex/base64), indentation indicators `|2`, double-quoted escapes (`\\\\x41` `\\\\u0041` `\\\\U..` `\\\\n`, line-folding with trailing `\\\\`), single-quoted `''`, plain multi-line scalars, anchors `&d` + aliases `*d` + merge keys `<<: *base` (descriptor defined in one job, used in another), `!!binary` (base64 -> bytes), `!!str`, flow maps/sequences `{X: \\\"..\\\"}`/`[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]` with a join step, comments after values, multi-document `---`/`...`, CRLF. Also the marker split across several `#` comment lines. Gate: each twist applied to the D21 members peels back to the same plan; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"git-repo-hooks-route\",\"concept\":\"repository-level auto-run surfaces: git hooks, filter/diff drivers, husky, pre-commit, devcontainer, submodules\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Supply-chain persistence next to CI: repo_hooks(members)->[{surface, trigger, command, lang}]: `.git/hooks/{pre-commit,post-checkout,post-merge,pre-push}` (shebang -> lang), `.git/config` `[core] hooksPath`, `[filter \\\"x\\\"] clean/smudge = ..` + `.gitattributes` `* filter=x`, `[diff \\\"x\\\"] textconv`, `[core] fsmonitor = ..`, `.husky/*`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` `repos[].hooks[].entry` + `language:`, `.gitmodules` url/update=!cmd, `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` postCreate/postStart (reuse json_scripts), `.vscode/tasks.json` `runOn: folderOpen`. ATT&CK hints T1195.002, T1546 (event-triggered), T1059.x. Gate: synthetic repo fixtures; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"launchd-plist-route\",\"concept\":\"macOS launchd / plist persistence (XML and binary plist)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"OS-side 'keeps coming back' sibling of D13 AppleScript. plist_scripts(name, data)->[{label, program_arguments, run_at_load, keep_alive, start_interval, lang}] for XML plists (`<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/bin/sh</string><string>-c</string><string>..</string>`) and binary `bplist00` (pure-Python parser: offset table, object refs; ints, strings ASCII/UTF-16BE, arrays, dicts, data, bools), `LaunchAgents`/`LaunchDaemons` path hints, `osascript -e` bodies -> AppleScript route. ATT&CK T1543.001/.004, T1647. Gate: plistlib-generated XML+binary fixtures round-trip (plistlib is stdlib; check ALLOWED_IMPORTS, else hand-parse).\"}\n]\nf